<urn:anqr:product-model-vocabulary:1> <urn:usf:predicate:canonicalName> "anqr-product-model-vocabulary" <urn:anqr:graph:product-model-vocabulary> .
<urn:anqr:product-model-vocabulary:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "No experience vocabulary is declared here. Experience travels through the existing uisemantics facet kind, of which the released product lane already satisfies seventeen; inventing a parallel experience layer would be exactly the duplication the ownership rule forbids." <urn:anqr:graph:product-model-vocabulary> .
<urn:anqr:product-model-vocabulary:1> <urn:usf:predicate:nonClaim> "ProductLifecycleStage is a deployment activity, not a second Semantic Build lifecycle. Each of its four values carries a semanticStage edge to the Foundation stage it belongs to, so build and deploy are realisation, and validate and operate are validation." <urn:anqr:graph:product-model-vocabulary> .
<urn:anqr:product-model-vocabulary:1> <urn:usf:predicate:objective> "Vocabulary for ANQR's own product model. It declares only what the corpus does not already carry, and instantiates rather than duplicates the Foundation's Semantic Build lifecycle, environments and facet machinery." <urn:anqr:graph:product-model-vocabulary> .
<urn:anqr:product-model-vocabulary:1> <urn:usf:predicate:type> <urn:usf:type:ProductModelDeclaration> <urn:anqr:graph:product-model-vocabulary> .
